  close:["The thing worth carrying away is not the numbers. It is that a society with no writing built a transmission system so exact that comparison of separately maintained branches still shows agreement down to the accent — and that it did so because it believed the **sound** of the text, not merely its meaning, was what had to survive.",
         "**Every other work in this section was written by somebody who wanted to be read. This one was made by people who wanted to be heard, exactly, by students who would repeat it to students they would never meet.** On the evidence, that turned out to be the more durable technology."]
